#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:5
#: df89745c3cda46be8401b4fb6d838bc8
msgid "Auto Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:7
#: 464c9ac09cf84d0aa4ea9fe9b9dd6be1
msgid "In Auto mode the copter will follow a pre-programmed mission script stored in the autopilot which is made up of navigation commands (i.e. waypoints) and \"do\" commands (i.e. commands that do not affect the location of the copter including triggering a camera shutter). This page provides an overview of  Auto mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:13
#: 06c47bb1168b452ab8232ce8e4583e87
msgid "Information on creating a mission script, can be found on the :ref:`Planning a mission with waypoints and events <common-planning-a-mission-with-waypoints-and-events>` page. A full list of supported commands can be found on the :ref:`Mission Command List <mission-command-list>` page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:17
#: 0a1644530c994d33abc57d12817f6e95
msgid "AUTO mode incorporates the altitude control from :ref:`AltHold mode <altholdmode>` and position control from :ref:`Loiter mode <loiter-mode>` and should not be attempted before these modes are flying well.  All the same requirements apply including ensuring that :ref:`vibration levels <common-measuring-vibration>` and compass interference levels are acceptable and that the GPS is functioning well including returning an HDOP of under 1.4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:25
#: 86a67b6a739e4504aaed66140ae81af4
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:30
#: d4462a0a6b6f49d4b62386fe45fc1d8c
msgid "AUTO mode navigates between each waypoint in a straight line and as it approaches each waypoint follows a smooth curving path towards the next waypoint (S-Curve). It controls the path as it approaches a waypoint to be within the :ref:`WP_RADIUS_M<WP_RADIUS_M>` of each waypoint. The speed is lowered below :ref:`WP_SPD<WP_SPD>`, as necessary, to keep the vehicle within the configured acceleration limits (:ref:`WP_ACC<WP_ACC>` and :ref:`WP_ACC_CNR<WP_ACC_CNR>`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:32
#: 481e0d7e6a2f4a98af954b8cc27c1cd6
msgid "This smooth curving path as it changes direction to the next waypoint will not occur if the next mission command after the waypoint is anything other than a normal waypoint (e.g LAND, LOITER_TURNS, RTL, etc). In these cases the copter will approach the waypoint, stop, and then proceed to the next navigation waypoint instead of smoothly curving in front of it and proceeding to that next navigation waypoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:34
#: 9668f15caf6e448c8659a0da2210cb84
msgid "Also, small :ref:`WP_RADIUS_M<WP_RADIUS_M>` values will require that the curve be very small, effectively appearing like the non-S-Curve behavior explained above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:37
#: 8a76aaebd2e9441f89268f219b59e1c0
msgid "Starting a Mission"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:39
#: 860e207aa6f54b9da8b0ae4729ea940e
msgid "Missions can be entered and amended through the Mission Planner's Plan screen.  In general most missions begin with a Takeoff command, include a series of waypoints followed by a Return-To-Launch command.  Please refer to the :ref:`Mission Command List wiki page <mission-command-list>` for a list of supported commands along with a short description of each."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:41
#: 7b644d365bd4403e95f0a2a644a5ed5c
msgid "AUTO should be set-up as one of the :ref:`Flight Modes <flight-modes>` on the flight mode switch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:43
#: e404cd8dffb44004b288b861ea5782c2
msgid "By default the vehicle cannot be armed in Auto mode meaning the pilot must first :ref:`arm the motors <arming_the_motors>` in another mode before switching to Auto mode.  The :ref:`AUTO_OPTIONS <AUTO_OPTIONS>` parameter can be used to alter this behaviour, allowing arming while in AUTO mode, and/or, allowing a mission takeoff command to start as soon as the vehicle enters AUTO mode, even if the throttle has not been raised."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:45
#: 0cdbd9c817c441a686b953f8b3883fc6
msgid "If starting the mission while the copter is on the ground the pilot should ensure the throttle is down, then switch to the Auto flight mode, then raise the throttle.  The moment that the throttle is raised above zero, the copter will begin the mission."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:50
#: 5415509d8b3c4255a03c27cfa9abf6f7
msgid "If starting the mission while the vehicle is already flying, the mission will begin from the first command as soon as the vehicle is switched into Auto mode. If the first command in the mission is a take-off command but the vehicle is already above the take-off command's altitude the take-off command will be considered completed and the vehicle will move onto the next waypoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:57
#: fea87373a29a4dad9fc7a1a279c76584
msgid "At any time the pilot can retake control from the autopilot by returning the flight mode switch to another flight mode such as Stabilize or Loiter.  If the pilot then switches to AUTO again, by default the mission will resume from the last command unless :ref:`MIS_RESTART <MIS_RESTART>` has been set to \"1\" in which case the mission will restart from the first command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:62
#: dc844891b36348f68062c665f5c12a50
msgid "During the mission the pilot's roll, pitch and throttle inputs are ignored but the yaw can be overridden with the yaw stick.  This allows the pilot to, for example, aim the nose of the copter (which might have a hard mounted camera on it) as the copter flies the mission.  The autopilot will attempt to retake yaw control as the vehicle passes the next waypoint.  The :ref:`AUTO_OPTIONS <AUTO_OPTIONS>` param can be set to always ignore pilot yaw input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:70
#: 1d3adee06c184d008d5a31ded1675ffc
msgid "Ending a Mission"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:72
#: 933c9b15ea8046968cd6f12c7d20b3cc
msgid "Missions should normally have an RTL as their final command to ensure the copter will return after the mission completes.  Alternatively the final command could be a LAND with a different location.  Without a final RTL or LAND command the copter will simply stop at the final waypoint and the pilot will need to retake control with the transmitter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:78
#: c5d9359ada28458bbf8072047f441443
msgid "Remember that when using RTL, the copter will return to the \"home\" position which is the location where the copter was armed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:81
#: 3527c4bfc9cc45fb8490501946962c7f
msgid "As the copter touches down at the end of the mission the vehicle should automatically disarm but occasionally the vehicle may not sense the landing and the pilot may need to hold the throttle down and takeoff in another mode like Stabilize or Loiter and then manually disarm the vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:83
#: c88c51428a784336b360dc5a71699c2d
msgid "for a NAV_LAND, the :ref:`LAND_SPD_MS<LAND_SPD_MS>` and the :ref:`LAND_SPD_HIGH_MS<LAND_SPD_HIGH_MS>` parameters affect descent speed just like in the :ref:`land-mode`. The :ref:`PILOT_THR_BHV<PILOT_THR_BHV>` option bit 1, when set, allows high throttle stick position to cancel the landing, switching the vehicle to :ref:`Loiter<loiter-mode>` or :ref:`AltHold<altholdmode>` if Loiter is unavailable. During landing the pilot can re-position the vehicle using the pitch and roll sticks to avoid obstacles unless the :ref:`LAND_REPOSITION <LAND_REPOSITION>` parameter is changed to \"0\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:86
#: b0afba13c12c4f258fc66ecd25743268
msgid "Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:91
#: a4e8aefddf594de4bdbd2290163bc934
msgid "AUTO mode incorporates the altitude control from :ref:`AltHold mode <altholdmode>` and position control from :ref:`Loiter mode <loiter-mode>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:93
#: 1a3d2af240a7486785f65d2767a5f252
msgid "Commonly adjusted settings are listed below.  Most of these can be adjusted from the Mission Planner's Config, Extended Tuning screen (see above)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:95
#: c5618e44f14e4e0f8db3b3ad53e190af
msgid ":ref:`WP_SPD<WP_SPD>` is the maximum horizontal speed (in m/s) during missions.  The default is 10 which is 10m/s.  A typical copter can reach top speeds of 10m/s ~ 20m/s before it becomes unable to maintain both altitude and horizontal speed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:96
#: 6b029cc235cb4e19ae0eb9644ac57acb
msgid ":ref:`WP_ACC<WP_ACC>` determines how quickly the horizontal speed can change (in m/s/s).  Lower values result in smoother acceleration and deceleration and may also cause the vehicle to cut the corners more.  Higher values will lead to more aggressive movements and tighter cornering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:97
#: 7bcbd8d93644473a9e91b12190680fef
msgid ":ref:`WP_SPD_UP<WP_SPD_UP>` determines the max speed up in m/s.  Low values may lead to the vehicle's horizontal speed slowing during diagonal climbing waypoint segments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:98
#: fb4e750b6d7d4470ad174762446dad14
msgid ":ref:`WP_SPD_DN<WP_SPD_DN>` determines the max speed down in m/s.  Low values may lead to the vehicle's horizontal speed slowing during diagonal descending waypoint segments.  High values (above 150) may lead to unstable vertical descents as the vehicle passes through its own prop wash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:99
#: 965a44ec05ed4360bc25602aa8589d1c
msgid ":ref:`WP_RADIUS_M<WP_RADIUS_M>` allows you to control how close the copter must come to the waypoint before it is considered \"complete\" and the copter moves onto the next waypoint.  Setting this to a larger value may cause the vehicle to cut the corners more leading to a smoother path"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:101
#: ec8fc2f858c047fd8a985b377f65608e
msgid "Less commonly adjusted parameters include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:103
#: 5b7d921febc34bfd9df83e8ccb758d79
msgid ":ref:`WP_ACC_CNR<WP_ACC_CNR>` determines the maximum cornering acceleration in m/s/s.  Higher values will cause the vehicle to make sharper corners meaning it will cut the corners less"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:104
#: 0ec96dd6374d401db8a99886b9fa4add
msgid ":ref:`WP_ACC_Z<WP_ACC_Z>` determines how quickly the vertical speed can change"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:105
#: 36caf85971df4be8bc6c632c272b2c5e
msgid ":ref:`WP_JERK<WP_JERK>` determines how quickly the horizontal acceleration can change (in m/s/s/s).  Lower values will lead to a smoother acceleration and deceleration but will also lead to the mission taking slightly longer to complete"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:108
#: b892257049134e05ba5792660cec2b41
msgid "Common Problems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:110
#: 0afbfe62fafa47e78570a88b029ae9e2
msgid "Below are a list of commonly reported problems and recommendations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:112
#: d780dd3a98f647a78d5f1190ae10bea4
msgid "The vehicle does not cut the corners as much as I would like and/or stops at each waypoint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:114
#: 00dd923d63394c53ab9a6498694e3872
msgid "Increase :ref:`WP_RADIUS_M<WP_RADIUS_M>` to allow the vehicle to pass further from each waypoint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:115
#: d5691c5713bd427ea61a45ac829476f7
msgid "Increase :ref:`WP_SPD<WP_SPD>` to cause the vehicle to start turning earlier in order that it not surpass the max acceleration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:116
#: 72cc1c8ba8c24ecebe850e8cd22fe2ff
msgid "Decrease :ref:`WP_ACC<WP_ACC>` to cause the vehicle to start turning earlier and more gradually"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:117
#: 0a02c5b337b246d2a6d5d99974b6d0cb
msgid "Decrease :ref:`WP_ACC_CNR<WP_ACC_CNR>` or reset to the default of zero"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:118
#: 77814d24ee8946f3bb63744e877460b1
msgid "Ensure the waypoint command's Delay field is 0.  A delay of even 1 second will cause the vehicle to stop at the waypoint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:119
#: 7adff231b8b2490faada008768e31228
msgid "If :ref:`Dijkstras object avoidance <common-oa-dijkstras>` is enabled, by default the vehicle will stop at each waypoint.  This can be avoided by setting the :ref:`OA_OPTIONS <OA_OPTIONS>` parameter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:121
#: 215273345e8e45428c1627e4302352c0
msgid "The vehicle does not reach the configured maximum horizontal speed (e.g. :ref:`WP_SPD<WP_SPD>`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:123
#: 773f42631eaf4c38b39e8cfe7741be66
msgid "Increase :ref:`WP_ACCEL <WP_ACCEL>` to allow the vehicle to accelerate to its maximum speed more quickly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:124
#: 505b0ca1bb6e429f8a3336cdc6f9966f
msgid "Increase :ref:`WP_JERK <WP_JERK>` to allow the vehicle to get to its maximum acceleration more quickly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:125
#: df1169291db047adb53591b59cf91644
msgid "If the waypoint includes a climb or descent the vehicle's horizontal speed may be limited by :ref:`WP_SPD_UP <WP_SPD_UP>` or :ref:`WP_SPD_DN <WP_SPD_DN>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:126
#: 03431e9f315b409683befa35f932ce14
msgid "Ensure the vehicle's maximum lean angle (e.g. :ref:`ATC_ANGLE_MAX<ATC_ANGLE_MAX>`) is sufficient to reach the desired speed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:127
#: 9ebd5dbf0c484a819dd0173098f26b52
msgid "Ensure the vehicle has enough power to maintain both altitude and the desired speed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:128
#: f07422fea6274f6d9710ca5349f75086
msgid "If the mission command uses :ref:`terrain following <terrain-following>` the vehicle may need to slow horizontally to maintain the desired altitude above terrain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:129
#: 7f931d5c388f49e2afda4de577dcab16
msgid "Move the waypoints to be further apart.  S-Cruve navigation only looks forward two waypoints and plans a path that allows it to stop by the time it reaches the 2nd waypoints (`see this issue for more details <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/issues/28953>`__)"
msgstr ""
